LoRA and QLoRA on REVE work without naming the layers to adapt: the Hugging Face backend's default `lora_target_modules` is `"all-linear"`, as in the braindecode backend and `LoRAConfig`. It was `("query", "value")`, names REVE's layers do not have (they are `to_qkv` and `to_out`), so a REVE fine-tune given no `lora` settings failed with `Target modules {'value', 'query'} not found in the base model`.
